Subject: [PATCH] Hide the password manager row that cannot work

IsPasswordManagerAvailable() is false for every unbranded build because the
backend class it checks for is Google-internal, so the row only ever showed
"Stopped working on this device" and a picker behind it. The Local vault
extension replaces it, so the dead row goes away instead of lying.
---
diff --git a/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/autofill/settings/AutofillAndPasswordsFragment.java b/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/autofill/settings/AutofillAndPasswordsFragment.java
--- a/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/autofill/settings/AutofillAndPasswordsFragment.java
+++ b/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/autofill/settings/AutofillAndPasswordsFragment.java
@@ -190,6 +190,10 @@ public class AutofillAndPasswordsFragment extends ChromeBaseSettingsFragment {
         PasswordsPreference passwordsPreference = findPreference(PREF_PASSWORDS);
         passwordsPreference.setProfile(getProfile());
         passwordsPreference.setManagedPreferenceDelegate(createManagedPreferenceDelegate());
+        // The Play services password manager cannot exist in an unbranded build, so this
+        // row would only ever read "Stopped working on this device". The Local vault
+        // extension owns password storage instead.
+        passwordsPreference.setVisible(PasswordManagerUtilBridge.isPasswordManagerAvailable());
         passwordsPreference.setOnPreferenceClickListener(
                 preference -> {
                     recordCategoryLinkClick(YourSavedInfoDataCategory.PASSWORD_MANAGER);
